lking Tour","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2020-08-13","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Observe from the appropriate public path; do not enter the coop or handle animals. The official tour explicitly invites a stop.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"clmoa-student-admission","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Claremont Lewis Museum of Art","title":"See the Claremont Lewis Museum of Art","subtitle":"200 W. First Street, Claremont","notes":"Bring your student ID, browse the current exhibition at your own pace, and pair the visit with a walk through the adjacent Claremont Village.","short_summary":"A Claremont Depot museum with free student admission.","evidence_claim":"The Claremont Lewis Museum of Art lists general admission as free for students.","source_url":"https://clmoa.org/visit/","source_title":"Plan Your Visit","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Students are admitted free; check the museum’s current open days and bring student identification if requested.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fourth-saturdays-poetry","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Fourth Saturdays Poetry Readings","title":"Listen at Fourth Saturdays Poetry","subtitle":"Claremont Helen Renwick Library, 208 N. Harvard Ave.","notes":"Check the next reader lineup, arrive for the scheduled afternoon start, and stay afterward to discuss a poem or meet other attendees.","short_summary":"A recurring public poetry-reading series at the Claremont library.","evidence_claim":"The Friends of the Claremont Library describes Fourth Saturdays Poetry Readings as free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://www.claremontlibrary.org/monthly-poetry-readings.html","source_title":"Fourth Saturdays Poetry Readings","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":"2026-07-25","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free and open to the public; confirm the upcoming date because the series schedule can change.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"claremont-on-the-same-page","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Claremont: On the Same Page Community Read","title":"Join an On the Same Page event","subtitle":"Claremont Helen Renwick Library and local venues","notes":"Read as much of the selected book as you like, then choose a related talk or discussion from the community-read event schedule.","short_summary":"Free public programs built around Claremont’s annual community read.","evidence_claim":"The Friends of the Claremont Library states that all events for its 2025–2026 Claremont Community Read are free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://www.claremontlibrary.org/on-the-same-page.html","source_title":"On The Same Page","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free and open to the public; the book may be obtained separately, but attendance at the listed events requires no purchase.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"pitzer-campus-walking-tour","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Pitzer College walking tour","title":"Walk Pitzer’s mural-filled campus","subtitle":"Begin at Admission Plaza, Pitzer College","notes":"Start at Admission Plaza and follow the College’s walking-tour route through Holden Garden, Mead Hall, the Mounds, and the Academic Quad.","short_summary":"A self-directed route through named Pitzer campus landmarks.","evidence_claim":"Pitzer publishes a walking-tour guide that begins at Admission Plaza and directs visitors through Holden Garden, Mead Hall, the Mounds, and the Academic Quad.","source_url":"https://www.pitzer.edu/documents/pitzer-